# kex: skip-beam
# A crash inside a spawned process is reported as the CRASH, not as the
# scheduler's view of what happened next (kexhq/kex#174).
#
# The child's error used to be discarded outright — `catch (...) { exitValue =
# none }` — so the parent blocked forever on a reply that could never come and
# the program reported `deadlock: no process is runnable` at `:0:0`. Same
# defect, same line of code as in the main process, but with no message, no
# receiver type and no location.
#
# BEAM already reported the real error here, so this is also a backend-parity
# fix; it is `skip-beam` only because the two spell the report differently — an
# Erlang error report against a Kex diagnostic — not because BEAM gets it
# wrong.

type Msg = | Ping(Process)

main do
  let worker = spawn do
    receive do
      Ping(who) => who.send(10 / 0)
    end
  end

  worker.send(Ping(Process.self))
  receive do
    reply => IO.printLine("got ${reply}")
  end
end
